[ti:The Battle Hymn of the Republic]
[ar:Traditional]
[00:30.00]Mine eyes have seen the glory of the coming of the Lord
[00:54.00]He is trampling out the vintage where the grapes of wrath are stored
[01:06.00]He hath loosed the fateful lightning of His terrible swift sword
[01:09.48]His truth is marching on
[01:15.92]Glory, glory, hallelujah
[01:23.20]Glory, glory, hallelujah
[01:36.68]Glory, glory, hallelujah
[01:42.68]His truth is marching on
[02:12.66]I have seen Him in the watch fires of a hundred circling camps
[02:21.32]They have builded Him an altar in the evening dews and damps
[02:51.20]I can read His righteous sentence by the dim and flaring lamps
[03:03.88]His day is marching on
